5. ONBOARDING — BUILDING THE READING HABIT

The first-time user experience is extremely important.

Do not immediately show a complicated dashboard.

Guide the user through a short, friendly onboarding process.

The onboarding should explain that the objective is to build a habit that lasts, not to choose the largest possible daily goal.

Step 1: Welcome

Suggested Arabic copy:

“خلينا نبني عادة قراءة قرآن تقدر تستمر عليها كل يوم.”

Explain that small, consistent actions are welcome.

Step 2: Choose the daily reading goal

Ask:

“تحب تحدد وردك اليومي بإيه؟”

Give the user two options:

Option A: By pages

* Half a page.
* One page.
* Two pages.
* Three pages.
* Custom quantity.

Option B: By time

* 2 minutes.
* 5 minutes.
* 10 minutes.
* 15 minutes.
* Custom duration.

The user must choose either pages or minutes as the primary daily goal.

Important goal-setting guidance

Before confirming the goal, display a short explanation:

“اختار كمية تقدر تحافظ عليها حتى في الأيام المزدحمة، مش كمية تحسسك بالإنجاز في يوم واحد.”

Do not pressure users into choosing ambitious quantities.

Allow users to change their goals at any time.

Step 3: Introduce the Two-Minute Rule

Explain that even on difficult days, the user can maintain the habit by reading for only two minutes.

The minimum goal must be easy to access.

Do not force users to complete their normal reading goal when they are having a difficult day.

Step 4: Habit Stacking

Ask:

“إيه الفعل اللي بتعمله كل يوم ونقدر نربط قراءة القرآن بيه؟”

Offer suggestions:

* After Fajr prayer.
* After breakfast.
* After lunch.
* After Isha prayer.
* Before going to sleep.
* After waking up.
* After another user-defined daily activity.

Allow custom activities.

Help the user create a personal habit statement:

“بعد ما أخلص [العادات اليومية المختارة]، هقرأ [الورد اليومي] من القرآن.”

This should be saved in Firestore.

Step 5: Preferred reading time

Ask:

“إمتى تحب تقرأ وردك؟”

Allow:

* Selecting a suggested time.
* Choosing a custom time.
* Changing it later.

The user can choose both a daily routine trigger and a preferred clock time.

Do not make either option mandatory if the user prefers flexibility.

Step 6: Notification permission

Explain the benefits of reminders before requesting browser notification permission.

Do not request notification permission immediately upon opening the website.

Ask only after the user understands the feature.

The user must be able to skip this step.

