7. DON’T MISS MODE — THE TWO-MINUTE RULE

This is one of the most important product features.

The purpose is to help users avoid skipping their reading habit entirely when the day is almost over or when they have limited time.

Concept

If the user feels that the day is ending and they have not read their Quran portion, they can activate Don’t Miss Mode.

The system should make this action effortless.

User experience

Display a prominent option:

“لسه مفيش وقت؟ اقرأ دقيقتين بس.”

When activated:

1. Open the Quran reader.
2. Resume from the last saved reading position.
3. Start a two-minute timer.
4. Encourage the user to read without pressure.
5. Allow the user to continue after the timer finishes.
6. Save the session automatically.

Completion

When two minutes are completed:

Display a gentle message:

“الحمد لله، حافظت على عادة القراءة النهارده.”

Do not automatically mark the user’s normal daily goal as completed.

Keep the two achievement states separate:

* Normal daily goal completed.
* Minimum two-minute goal completed.

The user should be able to activate this mode manually whenever needed.

The system should not force this mode or automatically replace the user’s normal goal.

Important behavior

* No penalties.
* No accumulated missed goals.
* No forced compensation.
* No guilt-inducing messages.

The goal is to make starting easy.

