8. FLEXIBLE GOALS — ADJUSTING THE DAILY READING TARGET

Allow users to increase or decrease their daily reading goal according to their circumstances.

For example:

A user who normally reads two pages daily might temporarily reduce the goal to one page.

Another user might increase the target when they have more free time.

Required functionality:

* Edit the daily goal.
* Change between pages and minutes.
* Set a new quantity.
* Save changes automatically.
* Synchronize changes through Firestore.
* Reflect updated goals immediately on the dashboard.

Do not treat changing a goal as failure.

Avoid excessive warnings when users reduce their targets.

The user must remain in control.

