9. COMEBACK MODE — RETURNING AFTER INTERRUPTION

Create a dedicated feature called Comeback Mode.

Its purpose is to help users resume Quran reading after missing several days or losing their routine.

Concept

When a user returns after an interruption, the system should make restarting easy.

Suggested Arabic message:

“وحشتنا قراءتك. مش محتاج تعوض اللي فات، ابدأ من جديد بالقدر اللي يناسبك.”

Requirements

* Detect periods of reading inactivity.
* Offer a gentle comeback experience.
* Allow users to resume from their last reading position.
* Suggest returning with a manageable reading amount.
* Offer the two-minute option.
* Allow users to keep, reduce, or adjust their normal goal.

Do not create overdue reading tasks.

Do not add missed pages to future goals.

Do not display negative streak statistics.

The user must feel welcome to return at any time.

