1. Identify the exact Surah and Ayah.
2. Open a clean interpretation panel.
3. Retrieve the corresponding Tafsir Al-Saadi text.
4. Display the interpretation in Arabic.
5. Allow the user to close the panel and return to the same Quran page.

Design

On mobile:

* Use a bottom sheet or a suitable overlay.

On desktop:

* Use a side panel or centered dialog.

Keep the Quran page visible whenever practical.

Important requirements

* Use a reliable and authorized source for Tafsir Al-Saadi.
* Map each interpretation to the correct Surah and Ayah.
* Never invent or AI-generate the tafsir text.
* Preserve Arabic formatting.
* Clearly identify the source as Tafsir Al-Saadi.
* Show a loading state when fetching the interpretation.
* Handle unavailable interpretations gracefully.

Do not add a summary of Tafsir after the daily reading session.

The user explicitly wants the interpretation available when selecting an individual verse, not an automatically displayed post-reading summary.

