13. NOTIFICATIONS — BROWSER PUSH ONLY

The only approved reminder channel is Browser Push Notifications.

Do not implement email reminders.

Do not use in-app notifications as a separate reminder channel.

Use Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM).

Notification scenarios

A. Scheduled reading reminder

At the user’s preferred time, send a gentle reminder.

Example:

“حان وقت وردك اليومي. افتح المصحف وابدأ بالقدر اللي يناسبك.”

B. Missed scheduled reading time

If the user has not completed their goal after the scheduled reading time, a suitable reminder may be sent.

Example:

“لسه تقدر تقرأ وردك النهارده.”

C. End-of-day reminder

If the daily reading goal has not been completed, send a gentle reminder suggesting Don’t Miss Mode.

Example:

“اليوم لسه مخلصش. دقيقتين من القرآن ممكن يكونوا بداية جميلة.”

Notification logic

* Stop relevant reminders after the user completes the normal daily goal.
* Avoid unnecessary repeated notifications.
* Respect the user’s notification preferences.
* Allow the user to disable notifications.
* Handle notification permissions correctly.
* Respect the user’s local timezone.
* Avoid sending notifications at inappropriate hours.

Technical implementation

Implement:

* Firebase Cloud Messaging.
* Web Push notifications.
* Service Worker.
* FCM token registration.
* Secure token management.
* Firebase Cloud Functions for scheduling and checking notification eligibility.

Support browsers and devices that permit Web Push.

Account for platform-specific limitations, especially iOS browser notification requirements and installed Progressive Web App requirements.

Never promise push notifications on unsupported browser configurations.

Ask for permission only after explaining the feature.

